.TH TTY21 1 "2026-11-04" "tty21 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tty21 \- terminal blackjack roguelike
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tty21
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A roguelike deckbuilder based on blackjack, played in the terminal.
Defeat dealers, descend through floors, acquire perks, and adapt to changing
rules and boss encounters. A classic blackjack mode is also available.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show command-line help and exit.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-roguelike
Start a new roguelike run (the default).
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-classic
Start classic blackjack mode.
.TP
.B \-\-fast
Skip animation pauses.
.TP
.B \-\-continue
Load the last saved roguelike game.
.TP
.B \-\-seed
.I N
Use
.I N
as the RNG seed. The short form
.B \-s
is also supported; the long form may be written
.BR \-\-seed=N .
.TP
.B \-\-no-save
Disable autosaving for this session.
.SH CONTROLS
During the player's turn:
.TP
.B h
Hit.
.TP
.B s
Stand.
.TP
.B d
Double down, when eligible.
.TP
.B p
Split, when eligible.
.TP
.B u
Surrender, when eligible; half the bet is lost.
.TP
.B k
Peek at the dealer's hole card when the Peek perk or a free-peek event permits it.
.TP
.B q
Quit the current run and return to the main menu.
.PP
Use the arrow keys and Enter to navigate menus and select actions.
Press
.B ?
to display the in-game help overlay.
.PP
Between rounds, use
.B c
to continue,
.B a
to advance floors,
.B w
to save,
.B s
to open the shop, or
.B q
to quit the run.
.SH SAVING
Roguelike games are autosaved to
.BR $XDG_DATA_HOME/tty21/save.dat ,
or
.BR ~/.local/share/tty21/save.dat
when
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
is not set to an absolute path. Use
.B \-\-continue
to resume the saved game. Classic mode does not save. The
.B \-\-no-save
option disables saving for the session.
.SH AUTHOR
Written by NotVeranto.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR make (1)
